## Why This Is Asked

Safety-critical navigation in urban environments requires reliable 3D pose estimation and intent understanding from monocular video. A new angle tests on-device adaptation to unseen clothing and backpacks, plus robust temporal reasoning under occlusion, aligning with real-world edge deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation from a single RGB stream
- Pedestrian intent recognition for near-term collisions
- Edge latency constraints and adapter-based on-device learning
- Synthetic+real data strategies to cover diverse outfits and behaviors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion robustness in losses

## Code Example

```javascript
function computeLoss(outputs, targets) {
  const poseLoss = l2(outputs.pose, targets.pose);
  const intentLoss = crossEntropy(outputs.intent, targets.intent);
  const temporalLoss = smoothL1(outputs.posePrev, outputs.pose);
  return poseLoss + 0.5 * intentLoss + 0.2 * temporalLoss;
}
```

